ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA MAPPING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[x] Surface renders all web states. The web source composes only useTranslation + useId
    (NO fetch/query/cache/connectivity) — it is a write-only callback form whose render
    branches are: the editable note, the too-long validation error (trimmed > 1000), the
    in-flight submitting-disabled state, and the optional acked-alert subtitle. All four
    reproduced. loading/empty/error/stale/offline are deliberately ABSENT — they would be
    fabricated behavior the web source does not have (no network read) — reproduced
    faithfully, not invented (Honesty Covenant: no parity shortcuts / no silent drift).
[x] Hooks bind via the shared P1/S8 state-holder layer: AcknowledgeAlertDialogViewModel
    (over the ILocalizer facade). The ack mutation is owned by the parent (web AlertsPage),
    modeled as the AcknowledgeRequested(note) callback event. The view performs NO data access.
[x] Every i18n key from the web source has a matching key in the P1/S10 catalog and is
    resolved through the ILocalizer facade — verified present in Strings/en/Resources.resw:
      translation.alerts.ack.dialogTitle     = "Acknowledge alert"
      translation.alerts.ack.noteLabel       = "Note (optional)"
      translation.alerts.ack.notePlaceholder = "Optional: what's being done?"
      translation.alerts.ack.noteHint        = "Up to {0} characters. Shared in the audit timeline."
      translation.alerts.ack.cancel          = "Cancel"
      translation.alerts.ack.submit          = "Acknowledge"
